  "title": "Learner failing between NEWLEADER and UPTODATE leaks its request processors",
  "cause": "startupWithoutServing leaves the learner server INITIAL and canShutdown() accepts only RUNNING or ERROR, so Follower.shutdown() after a failure before UPTODATE does not stop the started processors.",
  "trigger": "Connection loss, timeout or exception after NEWLEADER and before UPTODATE, followed by the normal Follower.shutdown().",
  "consequence": "SyncThread and CommitProcessor threads keep running after shutdown, the data tree is not fast-forwarded, and the orphaned SyncThread keeps writing the shared log and ACKs to a dead connection.",
  "sites": [
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/ZooKeeperServer.java:784-786",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Learner.java:751"
  ],
  "actions": [],
  "invariants": [],
  "premises": [
    "QuorumPeer.run calls follower.shutdown() after every followLeader(); LearnerZooKeeperServer.shutdown returns early when canShutdown() is false."
  ],
